# src/api/schema.d.ts is deliberately NOT ignored, though it is generated.
#
# `npm run build` runs `tsc -b` first, and five files under src/api import from './schema'. The
# frontend image builds with only what is in the repository, so an ignored schema.d.ts means
# `docker compose build` fails on a fresh clone with "Cannot find module './schema'".
#
# Regenerating it on the server is not an option either: `npm run api:sync` fetches the spec from
# a running backend, and the backend is what the build is for. So the generated file is committed,
# alongside the openapi.json it came from, and both are refreshed by api:sync when the API changes.
